            <ArticleTitle>Mechanism of pain caused by the nerve-root tension test in patients with sciatica.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>601-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe 2 instances where sciatic nerve block prevented pain in the sciatic nerve distribution caused by the nerve-root tension test in patients with radiculopathy. We hypothesize that antidromic activation of nociceptors from the injured root is a mechanism underlying sciatica.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
